<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prizren</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prizren is a city in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosovo">Kosovo</a>, at the foot of the Šar Mountains. It was an important town of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> and later an Ottoman trading centre with mosques, a stone bridge and the Serbian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> church of Our Lady of Ljeviš. In 1878 Albanian leaders founded the League of Prizren there to resist the partition of Albanian lands, and the city is now the second largest in Kosovo.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prizren.jpg" alt="Prizren" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ShkelzenRexha · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:37_Prizreni_-_Xhamia_e_Sinan_Pash%C3%ABs_-_The_Sinan_Pasha_Moscue.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
